{"data": [{"author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-10-31T19:03:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116606900271788210"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 31, "id": "1873146060467818496", "start": 16, "username": "AnushElangovan"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/3al52CFQOt", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2116606900271788210/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116606897704898561", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/3al52CFQOt"}]}, "id": "2116606900271788210", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 27, "impression_count": 15696, "like_count": 196, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 34, "retweet_count": 12}, "text": "ALERT🚨🚨🚨: AMD's @AnushElangovan and his team have achieved up to 2x better performance per dollar than even B200 on Kimi K3 Agentic Inference! This is due to various software optimization efforts, including tuning AITER kernels and MonoKernel decode.\n\nAlong with MI355X having https://t.co/3al52CFQOt", "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2116606900271788210"}, {"author_id": "4783690002", "created_at": "2026-10-31T13:33:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116524000977285321"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/qab3z41WDa", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/GoogleDeepMind/status/2116524000977285321/video/1", "media_key": "13_2116523390362095616", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/qab3z41WDa"}]}, "id": "2116524000977285321", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 186, "impression_count": 62664, "like_count": 771, "quote_count": 71, "reply_count": 215, "retweet_count": 77}, "text": "We built PlanAssist to help UK Government planning officers speed up building and renovations across the country.\n\nBuilt with Gemini, it has shown it can cut the time planning officers spend assessing householder applications by up to 58%. It is now being made available to 12 https://t.co/qab3z41WDa", "url": "https://x.com/GoogleDeepMind/status/2116524000977285321"}, {"author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-10-31T02:28:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116356583634469122"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/AnthropicAI/st…", "end": 23, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/AnthropicAI/status/2115871889549865429?s=20", "start": 0, "url": "https://t.co/9vZuZo5iPT"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/jeFKWrKcZ9", "end": 47, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2116356583634469122/photo/1", "media_key": "16_2116356566030934016", "start": 24, "url": "https://t.co/jeFKWrKcZ9"}]}, "id": "2116356583634469122", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 15, "impression_count": 33168, "like_count": 124, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115871889549865429", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "https://t.co/9vZuZo5iPT https://t.co/jeFKWrKcZ9", "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2116356583634469122"}, {"author_id": "1353836358901501952", "created_at": "2026-10-31T01:59:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116349211549843666"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/jlmo21NCLZ", "end": 297, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/AnthropicAI/status/2116349211549843666/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116345448617459712", "start": 274, "url": "https://t.co/jlmo21NCLZ"}]}, "id": "2116349211549843666", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1141, "impression_count": 423943, "like_count": 3340, "quote_count": 281, "reply_count": 503, "retweet_count": 322}, "text": "New Anthropic research: Automating subtle emergent misalignment research.\n\nRed-teaming is a vital part of model safety testing, but it’s also limited by researchers’ time. To see if we could automate it, we set thousands of Claude agents the task of evading a training data https://t.co/jlmo21NCLZ", "url": "https://x.com/AnthropicAI/status/2116349211549843666"}, {"author_id": "985281530070265862", "created_at": "2026-10-31T01:55:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116348216300192245"], "id": "2116348216300192245", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 86, "impression_count": 88208, "like_count": 1415, "quote_count": 9, "reply_count": 54, "retweet_count": 32}, "text": "You gotta give props to George Bush\nHe went and fucked up the Middle East\nHe's not even in the Epteans files\nIt's just for love of the game", "url": "https://x.com/dylan522p/status/2116348216300192245"}, {"author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-10-30T23:00:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116304252565856470"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/Eh7IN1hhpT", "end": 161, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2116304252565856470/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116304249998946304", "start": 138, "url": "https://t.co/Eh7IN1hhpT"}]}, "id": "2116304252565856470", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 11, "impression_count": 31698, "like_count": 79, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 18, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "Canon just cut its 2026 i-line stepper plan for the second time this year. We believe share loss in China is one important driver. (1/5)🧵 https://t.co/Eh7IN1hhpT", "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2116304252565856470"}, {"author_id": "2939913921", "created_at": "2026-10-30T20:49:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116271281351881120"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/YLIQOmnnX7", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2116271281351881120/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116271278805893120", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/YLIQOmnnX7"}]}, "id": "2116271281351881120", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 405, "impression_count": 21797, "like_count": 416, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 30, "retweet_count": 32}, "text": "Was reading the score-centering RL paper to add some notes on it the my book, and they have a great table in the appendix on the different importance sampling based train-inference mismatch methods in RL. These have been the biggest focus of RL algorithm research since the GRPO https://t.co/YLIQOmnnX7", "url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2116271281351881120"}, {"author_id": "1529761561170124800", "created_at": "2026-10-30T19:41:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116254070944170440"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/jDdrktihTC", "end": 286, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EpochAIResearch/status/2116254070944170440/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116254067865669632", "start": 263, "url": "https://t.co/jDdrktihTC"}]}, "id": "2116254070944170440", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 26, "impression_count": 9742, "like_count": 161, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 24}, "text": "Acknowledgments of large language model (LLM) use in biology preprints have grown exponentially since 2023. In three years, the share of preprints acknowledging LLM use is nearly as high as acknowledgments of specialized AI tool use, at 17% vs. 19% in September. https://t.co/jDdrktihTC", "url": "https://x.com/EpochAIResearch/status/2116254070944170440"}, {"author_id": "4398626122", "created_at": "2026-10-30T19:38:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116253388883345623"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/19NY7tgPHM", "end": 75, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/OpenAI/status/2116253388883345623/video/1", "media_key": "13_2116236456897212416", "start": 52, "url": "https://t.co/19NY7tgPHM"}]}, "id": "2116253388883345623", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2235, "impression_count": 2293351, "like_count": 10589, "quote_count": 536, "reply_count": 847, "retweet_count": 721}, "text": "There are many futures. Which do you want to build? https://t.co/19NY7tgPHM", "url": "https://x.com/OpenAI/status/2116253388883345623"}, {"author_id": "2939913921", "created_at": "2026-10-30T18:07:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116230595219210284"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/natolambert/st…", "end": 244, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/natolambert/status/2116224502283772307", "start": 221, "url": "https://t.co/Kh7h1cp3BI"}]}, "id": "2116230595219210284", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 15, "impression_count": 7978, "like_count": 94, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 16, "retweet_count": 9}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116224502283772307", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Open models will be used for cyber attacks, just like closed models have been. At the same time, open models aren’t the super high leverage tool magically increasing cyber crime by 100x — those bottlenecks lay elsewhere. https://t.co/Kh7h1cp3BI", "url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2116230595219210284"}, {"author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-10-30T18:00:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116228729282125827"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/xMJHG1NPc2", "end": 288, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2116228729282125827/video/1", "media_key": "7_2116228697275392000", "start": 265, "url": "https://t.co/xMJHG1NPc2"}]}, "id": "2116228729282125827", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 44, "impression_count": 22558, "like_count": 72, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "How would Meta deploy its networking clusters? How would that be different at Oracle, Nebius or Crusoe?\n\nClara Ee on the SemiAnalysis AI Networking Model: a bottoms-up build of every buyer's clusters that gives the BOM of each one and the networking equipment TAM. https://t.co/xMJHG1NPc2", "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2116228729282125827"}, {"author_id": "2465283662", "created_at": "2026-10-30T17:50:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116226251941642405"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Join the discussion on this paper page", "display_url": "huggingface.co/papers/2610.38…", "end": 102, "expanded_url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.38568", "images": [{"height": 648, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116226254542106624/mtJGNiex?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116226254542106624/mtJGNiex?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 79, "status": 200, "title": "Paper page - A-RSI: Adaptive Task Refresh for Zero-Data Multimodal Self-Improvement", "unwound_url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.38568", "url": "https://t.co/nLGUxellGs"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/ksRcUckuGY", "end": 126, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/_akhaliq/status/2116226251941642405/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116226216424312832", "start": 103, "url": "https://t.co/ksRcUckuGY"}]}, "id": "2116226251941642405", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 42, "impression_count": 13216, "like_count": 59, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 13, "retweet_count": 8}, "text": "A-RSI\n\nAdaptive Task Refresh for Zero-Data Multimodal Self-Improvement\n\npaper: https://t.co/nLGUxellGs https://t.co/ksRcUckuGY", "url": "https://x.com/_akhaliq/status/2116226251941642405"}, {"author_id": "2939913921", "created_at": "2026-10-30T17:43:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116224502283772307"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Last week coined the term “Black October“ after an onslaught of critical vulnerability disclosures, including PHP2Shell and GitLab, signified the moment when the cyber risks of AI models started to materialize.", "display_url": "interconnects.ai/p/was-i-wrong-…", "end": 279, "expanded_url": "https://www.interconnects.ai/p/was-i-wrong-about-open-models-and", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116224507795144704/Qz1o3nwF?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1600}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116224507795144704/Qz1o3nwF?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 256, "status": 200, "title": "Was I wrong about open models & cyber risks?", "unwound_url": "https://www.interconnects.ai/p/was-i-wrong-about-open-models-and", "url": "https://t.co/oroORcuDWU"}]}, "id": "2116224502283772307", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 28, "impression_count": 16983, "like_count": 115, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 17, "retweet_count": 10}, "text": "Was I wrong about open models &amp; cyber risks? I don't think so. The AI community is focusing on the wrong lens  - which type of model is causing harm - rather than how cybersecurity maintains an equilibrium, who enacts harm, and how they use new tools.\nhttps://t.co/oroORcuDWU", "url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2116224502283772307"}, {"author_id": "4398626122", "created_at": "2026-10-30T15:12:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116186509384815084"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/RWhIX72c09", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/OpenAI/status/2116186509384815084/video/1", "media_key": "13_2116186389536788480", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/RWhIX72c09"}]}, "id": "2116186509384815084", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 536, "impression_count": 368012, "like_count": 2870, "quote_count": 182, "reply_count": 510, "retweet_count": 213}, "text": "Privacy should advance as fast as intelligence. OpenAI Private Intelligence gives businesses stronger controls over their data while using our most capable models.\n\nWe’re building these protections in close collaboration with some of our largest customers to help businesses apply https://t.co/RWhIX72c09", "url": "https://x.com/OpenAI/status/2116186509384815084"}, {"author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-10-30T15:08:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116185427593863556"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/i4XwPkAf9H", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2116185427593863556/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116185424188022784", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/i4XwPkAf9H"}]}, "id": "2116185427593863556", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 30, "impression_count": 20975, "like_count": 74, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 17, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "In Semicon west this year, there was a lot of buzz around hybrid bonding. EV group presented hybrid bonding as an important technique accelerating 3D integratio